<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Izborsk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Izborsk is an old village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pskov">Pskov</a> Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, near the Estonian border, and one of the oldest towns of the Rus'. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> names it among the towns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krivichs">Krivichs</a> and as the seat of Truvor, a brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik">Rurik</a>. Its stone fortress, built in the 14th century on a new site, guarded the western approaches to Pskov.</p></div>
